# The discourse words in use (Docs/Design/84 §10.3, Phase 7): move lines (no concept; found by the move they make, §8.2)
# said through the grammars' discourse symbols, so each speaker closes, refuses, gives ground, apologises and takes in
# news in their own dialect ("The lake waits for nobody, nor do I." / "Well. The stars move, and so must I."). They sit
# beside turns.talk's and beats.talk's plain lines, a choice among them; Phase 8 writes the rest of the shared lines
# with these symbols. Short (the often-said ones under six words), so seldom a "distinctive" line for the scorecard's R4
# and R5; a refusal is longer, as a dispreferred answer is (§7.2).

## Closing (§8.4)
rule ds_preclose
does preclose
when self.stage=adult|old
say #preclose#. | #excuse#.

# (Slice 3: a pup's excuse isn't the grown-ups' "Work won't wait." or "The shift won't wait.")
rule ds_preclose_young
does preclose
when self.stage=young|adolescent
say #preclose#.

## Refusals, softened and explained (§7.2: hedge, account, remedy)
rule ds_decline
does decline
say #hedge#. #account#. | #hedge#. #account#. #later.capitalize#, maybe.

rule ds_put_off
does put_off
say #hedge#. #put_off#. | #put_off#. #account#.

rule ds_accept_decline
does accept_decline
say #no_matter#.

## Requests
rule ds_go_ahead
does go_ahead
say #go_ahead#.

## Views (§8.8: the engine lets a disagreement through only where the stances differ)
rule ds_disagree
does disagree
say #hedge#. #demur#.

rule ds_concede
does concede
say #concede#.

rule ds_insist
does insist
say #insist#.

## Feelings
rule ds_sympathise
does sympathise
say #sympathy#.

rule ds_reassure
does reassure
say #reassure#.

rule ds_congratulate
does congratulate
say #congrats#!

## Apologies and thanks
rule ds_apologise
does apologise
say #sorry#.

rule ds_accept_apology
does accept_apology
say #forgive#.

rule ds_deflect_thanks
does deflect_thanks
say #deflect#.

## News one had (§8.6; never for a death or a hurt, which beats.talk's grave lines answer)
rule ds_known
does react.news.known
when self.knows=yes topic.claim_kind!=death|violence|victim
say #knew#.

## Taking in, coming back, a second meeting, a welcome
rule ds_ack
does ack
say #ack#.

rule ds_return
does return
say #resume#.

rule ds_again
does again.open
when pair.last_talk<0.3
cooldown 1d
say #welcome_back#?

rule ds_welcome_join
does welcome_join
say #welcome#.
